  "title": "Venezuela’s Delcy Rodríguez Defends US Oil Deal Amid Criticism",
  "summary": "Venezuela’s interim president, Delcy Rodríguez, defends the U.S.-Venezuelan oil deal that would secure 65 billion barrels of proven oil reserves, insisting the deal will preserve Venezuela’s sovereignty. However, the deal has sparked outrage in the country, with Rodríguez defending her government’s stance against the U.S. claims of control.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "Venezuela’s interim president, Delcy Rodríguez, defended the U.S.-Venezuelan oil deal with Donald Trump, claiming it would preserve ownership and sovereignty.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The U.S. claims to have majority control over Venezuela’s oil resources, while the deal reportedly secures 65 billion barrels of proven oil reserves.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Rodríguez, who assumed power after Trump ordered the abduction of Nicolás Maduro, took to the airwaves to address concerns about the deal’s implications.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
